// ─── style/no-raw-primitives ──────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Tag:      style
// Mechanism: GritQL (per-file, real-time)
// Blocking: Yes
//
// Prevents: Feature code reaching for the platform's raw building blocks
//           instead of the design system's primitives — bare `<div>` /
//           `<span>` / `<button>` on web, bare `View` / `Text` /
//           `Pressable` from `react-native` on native.
//
//           A raw element carries no token-aware defaults, so it is the
//           seam every off-system decision enters through: the moment a
//           model writes `<div>`, it must also invent the padding, the
//           color, and the type size — and it will invent them fluently
//           and slightly wrong. A primitive (`<Box>`, `<Text>` from your
//           own UI layer) accepts only token props, so the wrong value
//           does not typecheck. This is the load-bearing rule of the tag:
//           the others police escape hatches; this one closes the door
//           they leak through.
//
// Applies:  All component files EXCEPT:
//           - The primitives layer itself (it must use raw elements —
//             that is its whole job)
//           - Test files and scripts
//           - Documented render boundaries (see Adapt section 4)
//
// Error:    "Raw element — compose from the UI primitives instead
//            (Box/Stack for layout, Text for type), or use the
//            primitive's polymorphic prop when you need the semantic
//            element."
//
// ── Adapt ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// 1. Pick your arm. The two arms under `any` cover the two platforms;
//    DELETE the one that does not apply. A react-native-web project that
//    ships both surfaces keeps both — `any` (not `or`) is used precisely
//    so a tag matching neither list still falls through to the next arm
//    instead of short-circuiting the traversal.
//
//    - **Web / DOM** (the `$tag` arm): bans lowercase intrinsic JSX tags.
//      PascalCase component tags fall through automatically, so the tag
//      regex IS the ban list. Most projects also want `table`, `form`,
//      `label`, `input`, `select`.
//
//    - **React Native** (the `rn_primitive_import` arm): bans importing
//      core primitives from `react-native`. It keys on the import, not
//      the tag, because RN primitives are PascalCase and so are your own
//      components — `<View>` and `<Card>` are indistinguishable at the
//      tag level. The import is where they separate, and it is the
//      honest unit: a file that never imports `View` cannot render one.
//      Extend the identifier list with anything else your primitives
//      layer wraps (`FlatList`, `SafeAreaView`, `Modal`).
//
//      Note it does NOT ban the `react-native` module wholesale. Utility
//      APIs (`Platform`, `useWindowDimensions`, `StyleSheet`, `Linking`)
//      are legitimate in feature code; only the rendering primitives are
//      the design system's to own. `import type { ViewProps }` also
//      passes — a type import renders nothing.
//
// 2. Primitives-layer path (the `! $filename <:` exemption):
//    Point it at wherever your `<Box>` / `<Text>` live. Default is
//    `src/shared/ui/`. This exemption is mandatory — without it the rule
//    forbids the primitives from being implemented at all.
//
// 3. Polymorphism, not a second ban list:
//    Do not exempt semantic elements (`nav`, `section`, `li`) to keep
//    markup accessible. Give the primitive an `as` / `component` prop
//    typed as a closed union of allowed tags (`<Box as='nav'>`), so
//    semantics stay expressible without reopening an unconstrained
//    string surface. A closed union is a type-level guarantee; an
//    exemption list is a hole this rule cannot see through.
//
// 4. Render boundaries:
//    Some files legitimately emit raw elements — a markdown renderer's
//    element overrides, the root HTML document, a canvas-backed widget.
//    Exempt them by path, one line each, with a comment saying why. Each
//    exemption is a place drift can enter, so the reason should be about
//    the boundary, not about convenience.
//
// ── Implementation note ───────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The RN arm gates on a file-level regex rather than an import snippet
// because Biome's GritQL matches named-import snippets by ARITY:
// `import $_ from $source` matches `import { View } from "react-native"`
// but NOT `import { View, Text } from "react-native"`. Any rule keyed on
// a named-import snippet silently misses every multi-specifier import —
// a large hole, since that is the common shape. Verify this before
// writing any import-shaped rule. Grit regexes are anchored (full
// match), hence the `(?s).*` … `.*` wrapping.
//
// Diagnostics are spanned on the JSX tag, not the import, so the arrow
// lands on each use site and a type-only `import type { ViewProps }`
// never gets blamed.
//
// Known hole: namespace imports (`import * as RN from "react-native"`,
// then `<RN.View>`) are not matched by either arm. If your codebase uses
// that shape, ban it with a separate one-line rule rather than trying to
// thread it through here.
//
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

language js(typescript, jsx)

// An import statement pulling a rendering primitive out of react-native.
// `[^}]*` spans newlines, so multi-line (formatter-wrapped) imports match.
// `import\s*\{` requires the brace to follow `import` directly, which is what
// lets `import type { ViewProps }` through.
pattern rn_primitive_import() {
    r"(?s).*import\s*\{[^}]*\b(?:View|Text|Pressable|TouchableOpacity|ScrollView|TextInput|Image)\b[^}]*\}\s*from\s*\"react-native\".*"
}

file(name=$filename, body=$program) where {
    // --- Global exclusions (shared across all rules) ---
    ! $filename <: r".*\.test\.[tj]sx?$|.*\.integration\.test\.[tj]sx?$|.*__tests__.*|.*src/test/.*",
    ! $filename <: r".*/scripts/.*",

    // --- The primitives layer implements the primitives (Adapt 2) ---
    ! $filename <: r".*/src/shared/ui/.*",

    // --- Documented render boundaries (Adapt 4) ---
    ! $filename <: r".*/src/routes/__root\.tsx$",

    // Four shapes cover {self-closing, has-children} x {no attrs, attrs},
    // so the rule fires regardless of props or children.
    $program <: contains bubble($program) or {
        `<$tag />`,
        `<$tag $_ />`,
        `<$tag>$_</$_>`,
        `<$tag $_>$_</$_>`
    } where {
        any {
            // --- Web / DOM arm (Adapt 1) ---
            and {
                $tag <: r"^(?:div|span|p|main|section|header|footer|nav|aside|article|ul|ol|li|button|a|h1|h2|h3|h4|h5|h6|img)$",
                register_diagnostic(
                    span = $tag,
                    message = "Raw HTML element (highlighted) — compose from the UI primitives instead (Box/Stack/Group for layout, Text/Title for type, Button, Anchor, Image), or `<Box as='...'>` with the tag name when you need the semantic element. A raw element has no token-aware defaults, so every value on it has to be invented. See docs/architecture/design-system.md."
                )
            },

            // --- React Native arm (Adapt 1) ---
            // The tag names are gated on the file actually importing them from
            // react-native, so the app's OWN `<Text>` (from @/shared/ui) is not
            // caught by the shared name.
            and {
                $tag <: r"^(?:View|Text|Pressable|TouchableOpacity|ScrollView|TextInput|Image)$",
                $program <: rn_primitive_import(),
                register_diagnostic(
                    span = $tag,
                    message = "Core react-native rendering primitive (highlighted) — import the app equivalent from @/shared/ui instead (Box/Stack for View, Text for Text, a Button/Pressable wrapper for touchables). Those take token props, so an off-system value cannot be passed. Utility APIs from react-native (Platform, StyleSheet, useWindowDimensions) are fine in feature code; only the rendering primitives are the design system's to own. See docs/architecture/design-system.md."
                )
            }
        }
    }
}
